\begin_layout Standard
To achieve this, we developed a comprehensive verification environment combining
 a simulation testbench with the RISC-V GNU toolchain.
 Using this setup, we compiled C programs into RISC-V binaries that reflect
 realistic instruction mixes and execution patterns.
 These binaries were loaded into the processor’s memory, and the core was
 allowed to fetch, decode, and execute instructions autonomously.
 
